// Phase 4, slice 6, step 4 (#53): what is a signed-in maintainer's to act on,
// `GET /maintainers/mine`, against an in-memory D1 with the migrations
// applied. It's 12:00 UTC on 5 November; accuser is a maintainer (a kept
// membership answer), in public and private repositories alike.
suite github.hooks

stub Clock.now() returns Instant.fromEpochMillis(1793880000000)

---
accuser's open pull requests: #1 (CI failing on its head, though an older
commit passed), #2 (passing, after a failed first attempt), #3 a draft whose
only run lost its completion two days ago, and #4 in a private repository,
queued. #2 also has a lint run that lost its completion: it doesn't hold the
PR at "running". Someone else's #5 asks accuser (and a team) to review; #6
asks someone else; #7 is closed but still lists accuser. accuser's issues: #10
stale (no update since October), #11 fresh, and someone else's #12. Merges:
#20 after bynk-lang/bynk's latest final release, #21 before it, #22 already
shipped, #23 in a repository that never releases.
---
